<section class="panel" aria-label="Grade3 original 2021 quarter-inch measurement source-aligned tasks"><h2>Measure in Fourths of an Inch</h2>
<h3>Warm-up: paperclip estimate</h3><p>Estimate from source paperclip/ruler visual. Record a TOO LOW, JUST RIGHT and TOO HIGH guess. The original teacher's estimate is between 1 and1 1/2 inches, near1 1/4; this is not a verified physical measurement of the photograph.</p>
<h3>Activity1: Partition Inches into Fourths</h3><p>Work in pairs, reusing the <strong>whole-inch ruler left unpartitioned last lesson</strong>. Put three equal inside marks in EVERY inch: quarter, half, three quarters. Each partner chooses TWO different objects (four per pair) and records their real measured lengths to the nearest quarter-inch.</p>
