<h3>Activity2: Find Some Lengths</h3><p>Bring BOTH the old half-inch ruler and the quarter-inch ruler. Find <strong>at least four</strong> classroom objects fitting the original eight-row reference table. The eight rows are options, not eight mandatory separately found objects.</p>
<table class="source-chart"><thead><tr><th>Original length/category prompt</th><th>New first-party quarter-step model, if fixed</th><th>Real object found / actual length</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>2 1/2 inches</td><td>10/4 inches</td><td>______________</td></tr><tr><td>1 1/4 inches</td><td>5/4 inches</td><td>______________</td></tr><tr><td>3 3/4 inches</td><td>15/4 inches</td><td>______________</td></tr><tr><td>8 1/2 inches</td><td>34/4 inches</td><td>______________</td></tr><tr><td>a whole number of inches</td><td>Student-chosen whole number</td><td>______________</td></tr><tr><td>a whole number and 1/4 inches</td><td>Student-chosen whole number</td><td>______________</td></tr><tr><td>a whole number and 2/4 inches</td><td>Student-chosen whole number</td><td>______________</td></tr><tr><td>a whole number and 3/4 inches</td><td>Student-chosen whole number</td><td>______________</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>When a flexible last-four row is matched, write the COMPLETE mixed number. Teacher checks real-object ruler alignment, equal partition, correct unit and nearest-tick approximation.</p>
<p>Source synthesis compares whole-, half- and quarter-inch rulers. Quarter-inch markings offer finer resolution. The original teacher-only Cool-down and standalone pupil PDF have not been inspected; no publisher artwork copied. <a href="https://im.kendallhunt.com/k5/teachers/grade-3/unit-6/lesson-2/lesson.html">Original 2021 teacher lesson</a>.</p></section>